  "body": "## What changed\n\n- **`camcraft-tools::holder_library`** (new). A built-in library of steep-taper holders, drawn as spun profiles (#93). There are 36 entries, each a taper (BT30, BT40 or CAT40) with an ER collet chuck or a Weldon side-lock nose:\n  - **BT30:** ER16, ER20, ER25 and ER32; Weldon 6/8/10/12/16 mm and 1/4, 3/8, 1/2 in.\n  - **BT40:** ER16, ER20, ER25 and ER32; Weldon 6-20 mm and 1/4-3/4 in.\n  - **CAT40:** ER32; Weldon 1/4-3/4 in and 6-20 mm.\n\n  `HolderEntry::points(nose, gauge_len)` draws the outline tip-up: the nut (or Weldon body), the body to the flange, the flange as a full cylinder, the standoff to the gauge line, then closed at the gauge line. A gauge length that is too short, a non-finite number, or a shank the collet or bore can't take is refused by name.\n- **`SetToolBody::library(world, tool, entry, gauge_len, projection)`** (app). It drops a library entry into a tool's holder as one undoable command, built on `SetToolBody::spun`. The holder lands as a drawn profile and stays editable. The gauge length defaults to the entry's own. The projection (nose face above the tip) defaults to the tool's flute plus shank length. Collision checks judge it through the existing body path (`tool_body::judged` / `stack`), with no new collision code.\n- **Tool editor, Profile tab:** a \"Holder library\" section with a \"Library holder\" picker, a gauge length field, a one-line dimension summary, a live shank-fit refusal, and \"Apply holder\" (one undo step). After it lands, the holder edits as a Custom profile.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/793-taper-holders.md` has the dimension table, its sources, and the small-BT decision.\n\n## Dimension table (mm, summary; the sources are in the decision file)\n\n| Taper | Gauge Ø | Flange Ø | Gauge line to flange back | Flange thickness | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| BT30 | 31.75 | 46 | 2 | 20 | JIS B 6339 / MAS 403 |\n| BT40 | 44.45 | 63 | 2 | 25 | JIS B 6339 / MAS 403 |\n| CAT40 | 44.45 | 63.5 | 3.175 | 15.875 | ASME B5.50-2009 Table 1 |\n\nER nuts (DIN 6499 standard round nut; ISO 15488 collet ranges):\n\n| Size | Nut Ø × length | Collet range Ø |\n|---|---|---|\n| ER16 | 32 × 17.5 | 0.5-10 |\n| ER20 | 35 × 19.5 | 1-13 |\n| ER25 | 42 × 20 | 1-16 |\n| ER32 | 50 × 22.5 | 2-20 |\n\nWeldon bodies (DIN 1835 B bores, typical DIN 6359 bodies) run from Ø25 for the 6 mm bore to Ø52 for the 20 mm bore.\n\n**BT30 ER20** (the 770MX holder) at its default 60 mm gauge length:\n- ER20 nut Ø35 × 19.5;\n- body Ø35;\n- flange Ø46 × 20, with its front face 22 mm from the gauge line;\n- 2 mm standoff to the gauge line.\n\nThe flange's gripper groove and drive slots, the nut's chamfers and the body's neck are enveloped, never cut away. The taper inside the spindle is left out, so the spindle housing rides on the gauge line.\n\n**Small BT sizes (BT10/15/20/25):** not included. JIS B 6339 (ISO 7388) and ASME B5.50 start at size 30. No public standard table was found for the small sizes; their makers' dimensions differ. The decision file has the reasoning.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `camcraft-tools` (lib), `holder_library::tests`:\n  - `the_tapers_and_nuts_match_the_recorded_table`\n  - `the_bt30_er20_outline_is_the_table` (every point of the user's holder)\n  - `every_entry_draws_a_valid_profile_with_its_flange_and_nose`\n  - `a_longer_gauge_raises_the_flange_and_keeps_the_nose`\n  - `nonsense_is_refused_by_name`\n- `camcraft-app`, `tests/holder_library.rs`:\n  - `a_library_holder_lands_as_its_drawn_profile`\n  - `the_bt30_er20_flange_strikes_a_wall_the_cylinder_misses`: the plain Ø44 × 35 cylinder misses a wall at flange height, the BT30 flange strikes it, and a wall raised above the gauge line is clear.\n  - `a_long_gauge_weldon_clears_where_a_short_one_collides`\n  - `undo_restores_the_previous_holder`\n  - `nonsense_picks_are_refused_by_name`\n- `camcraft-ui` (lib, CWD crates/ui), `egui_app::tests::tool_holder` structural tests:\n  - `the_picker_stands_in_the_profile_tab_and_waits_for_a_pick`\n  - `apply_holder_lands_the_bt30_er20_and_undo_restores`\n  - `a_shank_the_holder_cannot_take_is_refused_by_name`\n- Regression suites: `tool_profile` (ui), `tool_spun_profile` and `tool_body` (app), and `structural` (ui) all pass.\n- Gates: the quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick`) is green, and so is clippy `-D warnings` on tools/app/ui. The Linux batch gate result is on the PR comments. No snapshot PNG changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No GUI hand check: the picker in the real app and the side view of a landed holder. The maintainer will check the BT30 ER20 against their real holder; nut and body diameters vary by maker, so expect the drawn nut to be the larger standard nut.\n- MCP: no tool sets a tool's holder today, so this is filed as #799 (\"MCP: set a tool's holder from the built-in holder library\").\n\nChangelog: Built-in holder library: BT30, BT40 and CAT40 taper holders in ER collet chuck and Weldon versions, picked in the tool editor's Profile tab and judged by the collision checks (#793)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.16.0.\n\nFixes #793\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
